# Mermaid — Cursor chat safe (mandatory)

Cursor IDE chat Mermaid renderer **fails** on `%%{init: ...}%%` theme JSON.
Agents repeatedly reintroduce it by copying old `document/*.md` examples.
**Never do that.**

## Hard rules (every chat, every diagram)

1. Fence starts with ` ```mermaid `, body is **diagram only**, then close the fence.
2. **Forbidden:** `%%{init`, `themeVariables`, `mainBkg`, any theme JSON.
3. **Forbidden:** Korean/English prose inside the fence (put it after the closing fence).
4. **Forbidden:** copying Mermaid with init from `document/` or archive — those examples are legacy for other viewers.
5. Labels short ASCII/words; avoid `<br/>` and nested quotes in node text.
6. Prefer `flowchart` / `sequenceDiagram` with `id[short label]` nodes.

## Template (copy this shape)

```mermaid
flowchart LR
  a[step one] --> b[step two]
  c[other] -.->|note| b
```

## If tempted to style

Do not. Transparent backgrounds are **not** worth Syntax Error. User already chose pure Mermaid for Cursor.
